								<div class="title" id="post-title-1341700">
																		Some detail about this SCP
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/misterbibs" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(453823); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=453823&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607267254" alt="MisterBibs" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=453823)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/misterbibs" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(453823); return false;" >MisterBibs</a></span> <span class="odate time_1325643776 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Jan 2012 02:22</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1341700">
									

<p>I always do one of these for an SCP, so I figured I'd do one for this one.</p>
<p>This SCP was inspired by a dream I had while I was sick a few weeks ago. Vaguely like <a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NM1r37zIBOQ&amp;feature=related" target="_blank">the Genesis Planet video in Wrath Of Khan</a>, but instead of fire or anything, it was nature. A tree sprung up, and then a wave of greenery covered the planet. Really strange dream, and it stuck with me enough to hammer something out as a rough SCP skeleton. Cut to a week later, when I'm blabbing about the dream to a friend of mine. He shrugged and said &quot;So you had a dream about <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dyson_tree" target="_blank">Dyson Trees</a>?&quot; I looked it up, and was shocked, since I've never seen anything like it before. I decided to keep working on the thing, because I liked the mystery of the idea. What is it? Who made it? Where did it come from? Why is it trying to do something with Earth? I chose the number 1923, since that Dyson guy was born in 1923.</p>
<p>The asteroid I used was <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/951_Gaspra" target="_blank">951 Gaspra</a>, which coincidentally is in the 'Flora' grouping.</p>

							</div>

								
